(7699130, 1263365, 60581, '<td valign="top">It was actually a water balloon and had a pin attached to the thumb using a Sellotape and when I was saying "GO" he was punching that pin against the balloon and had blast. since the shot was taken outside, it was sky reflection in the water was making it look bright/white so when I had hand in the front of the T-shirt and since the T-shirt was shite, those water splash was not showing as I wanted it to. Yes I could have used a red shirt or some dark shirt so that the water shows up but that all I observed when I was done with the shot and there was not any more any balloons left :D<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by vawendy:</b></div><hr/><i> Hmmm... something doesn''t feel right on this one. I''d be curious to see what it would have looked like if the person wasn''t so far to the side. The face isn''t quite out of focus enough, so it draws the eyes away from the interesting part of the photo. </i></td></tr></table></td>', 'It was actually a water balloon and had a pin attached to the thumb using a Sellotape and when I was saying "GO" he was punching that pin against the balloon and had blast. since the shot was taken outside, it was sky reflection in the water was making it look bright/white so when I had hand in the front of the T-shirt and since the T-shirt was shite, those water splash was not showing as I wanted it to. Yes I could have used a red shirt or some dark shirt so that the water shows up but that all I observed when I was done with the shot and there was not any more any balloons left :D Originally posted by vawendy: Hmmm... something doesn''t feel right on this one. I''d be curious to see what it would have looked like if the person wasn''t so far to the side. The face isn''t quite out of focus enough, so it draws the eyes away from the interesting part of the photo. ', '2021-08-17 10:57:33.000000', NULL, 0),
